{"step_index":3495,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:49:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T05:49:47-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-29T05:49:47-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/.agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 71\nTotal Bytes: 3808\nShowing lines 1 to 71\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: xmars-continuous-forge\n3: description: Autonomous 24/7 continuous training, synthetic distillation, blackbox discernment review, and Lead 9 council orchestration for XMARS and Xoras Systems.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # XMARS Continuous Forge Skill\n7: \n8: ## Overview\n9: The `xmars-continuous-forge` skill packages the entire sovereign hyper-accelerated synthetic training pipeline, autonomous governance, blackbox review engine, and Lead 9 council dispatching into an enterprise-grade agent workflow.\n10: \n11: Key Capabilities:\n12: - **Continuous Synthetic Training**: Mine repository code units and synthesize DPO paired corpora (chosen vs. rejected) to compress months of training into continuous fractional cycles.\n13: - **Autonomous Governance Supervisor**: 24/7 background supervisor maintaining hardware context boundaries (KV-cache flush, sliding windows, memory hygiene) at 180s cadences.\n14: - **Blackbox Discernment Audit**: William Vance's rigorous four-tier falsification engine evaluating candidates against Golden List standards.\n15: - **Council Dispatch & Studio Neural Vocalization**: Real-time token streaming and multi-tier neural voice playback across physical hardware DACs.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## Command-Line Tool: `scripts/xmars_forge.py`\n20: \n21: All operations are driven via the unified CLI script:\n22: `python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py <subcommand> [flags]`\n23: \n24: ### Available Subcommands\n25: \n26: | Subcommand | Description | Key Options |\n27: |------------|----------\n<truncated 577 bytes>\nonal neural speech | `<message>`, `--agent <name>`, `--speak`, `--output <file>` |\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## Usage Examples\n37: \n38: ### 1. Check Full Sovereign System Telemetry\n39: ```bash\n40: python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py status --output memory/agent_logs/forge_status.json\n41: ```\n42: \n43: ### 2. Trigger On-Demand Hyper-Accelerated Synthetic Training\n44: ```bash\n45: python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py train --cycles 1 --output memory/agent_logs/forge_train_result.json\n46: ```\n47: \n48: ### 3. Run Blackbox Review Engine\n49: ```bash\n50: python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py review ops/training/continuous_training_daemon.py --output memory/agent_logs/vance_audit.json\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ### 4. Inspect 24/7 Autonomous Supervisor Telemetry\n54: ```bash\n55: python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py supervisor --tail 5\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### 5. Dispatch Direct Task with Neural Studio Speech\n59: ```bash\n60: python .agents/skills/xmars-continuous-forge/scripts/xmars_forge.py dispatch \"Audit all active telemetry streams\" --agent Jarvis --speak\n61: ```\n62: \n63: ---\n64: \n65: ## Guidelines & Best Practices\n66: \n67: 1. **Output Redirection**: Always provide `--output <path>` when running inside automated scripts or agent invocations to preserve context space and log receipts canonically in `memory/agent_logs/`.\n68: 2. **Infrastructure Protection**: The core governance assets (`identity/charter.yaml`, `identity/lead9_roster.json`, `Xoras_agent_cards/`, `core_agents/`) are immutable and frozen under Log Entry #076.\n69: 3. **Audio Dispatch**: When `--speak` is enabled, the command uses Edge-TTS studio neural synthesis (`en-US-ChristopherNeural`, `en-US-GuyNeural`, etc.) with local Kokoro ONNX fallback.\n70: 4. **Autonomous Cadence**: The background supervisor runs on a strict 180s minimum interval to prevent GPU/CPU thrashing.\n71: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
